research/audit/wave5-topology-countability.provenance.jsonl:42:{"id": "ex-a-ccc-nonseparable-cantor-cube", "statement": "ai-generated", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "trivial", "urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_cube"], "rationale": "TRIVIAL, verification written out. The item is the single instantiation I = P(P(N)) of two results already on the page. Cantor's theorem (thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor clause (b)) gives |P(N)| = 2^aleph_0 and then |P(P(N))| = 2^(2^aleph_0) > 2^aleph_0, which is the hypothesis of both cited results; thm-cantor-cubes-are-ccc then gives ccc and lem-large-cantor-cubes-are-not-separable gives non-separability. Nothing is asserted beyond that substitution. Tagged ai-generated because the specific index set is a bespoke choice with no counterpart in a source, not because the mathematics is novel. BLAST RADIUS: zero - no item in the corpus has this id in its deps.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05", "generation_role": "example"}
