research/audit/wave5-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:25:{"id":"ex-contractive-sequence-fixed-point","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fixed-point_iteration","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contraction_mapping"],"rationale":"Positive novelty determination, on the witness. Linear fixed-point iteration u -> (u+1)/3 is an instance of a completely standard family (Wikipedia Fixed-point iteration; Contraction mapping), but no source selects THIS map, this constant, or this arbitrary starting value as its worked example; the map is chosen for this page so that the contraction inequality holds with EQUALITY at every index and c = 1/3 is therefore the smallest admissible constant. That is a bespoke checkable witness, which the AUDIT-WORKFLOW sect. 6 trivial row assigns to ai-generated with generation.role: example, following the wave-0 precedent Alpha upheld for cex-same-cardinality-without-a-canonical-bijection. Truth verified directly and completely from the stated dependencies: x_{k+2} - x_{k+1} = ((x_{k+1}+1) - (x_k+1))/3 = (x_{k+1} - x_k)/3, so |x_{k+2} - x_{k+1}| = (1/3)|x_{k+1} - x_k| exactly, giving contractivity with c = 1/3 in (0,1); thm-contractive-implies-cauchy then gives convergence to some L; the first tail has the same limit, so L = (L+1)/3, i.e. 3L = L+1, i.e. L = 1/2, for every starting value a. The remark's arithmetic also checks: x_1 = (a+1)/3, x_2 = (a+4)/9, so |x_2 - x_1| = |(1-2a)/9| = (2/9)|a - 1/2|. Blast radius nil: zero deps consumers corpus-wide. Recorded for Alpha as a borderline - ai-altered under an instance-of-a-standard-family reading is also defensible, and the label does not affect dependency eligibility here.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-05"}
research/audit/wave5-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:30:{"id":"cex-unbounded-with-convergent-subsequence","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolzano%E2%80%93Weierstrass_theorem","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subsequence"],"rationale":"Positive novelty determination, on the witness. That the converse of Bolzano-Weierstrass fails is established (and is tagged as such on the false statement this item refutes, fs-convergent-subsequence-implies-bounded), but the WITNESS is bespoke: the interleaving 1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 4, ... defined by cases on the even/odd partition of N supplied by lem-alternating-sequence, together with the computation that its subsequential limit set is exactly {1}. No source selects this construction; the item builds it from this page's own machinery. That is the bespoke checkable-witness species the AUDIT-WORKFLOW sect. 6 trivial row assigns to ai-generated with generation.role: counterexample, on the wave-0 precedent Alpha upheld. Truth verified directly from the stated dependencies: the definition is total and single-valued because e and o partition N and each is injective; the subsequence along o is constantly 1, hence convergent; for any real M the Archimedean property gives m >= 1 with |M| < m, and y_{e_{m-1}} = m > |M| >= M, so no M bounds |y_n|; and any convergent subsequence meets the range of e only finitely often (its values j+1 exceed every bound), so it is eventually constantly 1 and its limit is 1, giving SL = {1}. Blast radius nil: zero deps consumers corpus-wide. Recorded for Alpha as a borderline - ai-altered under established-knowledge is defensible if Alpha judges the interleaving itself to be canonical.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-05"}
research/audit/wave5-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:31:{"id":"cex-strictly-decreasing-gaps-no-limit","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contraction_mapping","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauchy_sequence"],"rationale":"Positive novelty determination, on the witness. That strictly decreasing gaps are strictly weaker than a uniform contraction constant is the standard caution attached to the contractive definition (Bartle-Sherbert sect. 3.5; Wikipedia Contraction mapping), but the WITNESS is bespoke: the recursion x_1 = 1, x_{k+1} = x_k + 1/x_k is a known recurrence with known asymptotics, and no source selects it to separate 'each gap smaller than the last' from 'contractive'. The construction, the induction g_j^2 >= 1 + 2j, and the divergence argument are written for this page. That is the bespoke checkable-witness species the AUDIT-WORKFLOW sect. 6 trivial row assigns to ai-generated with generation.role: counterexample. Truth verified directly from the stated dependencies: g takes values in {u : u >= 1}, so every gap d_j = 1/g_j is positive and the sequence strictly increases; 0 < g_j < g_{j+1} gives 0 < d_{j+1} < d_j, so the gaps strictly decrease; g_{j+1}^2 = g_j^2 + 2 + 1/g_j^2 > g_j^2 + 2 gives g_j^2 >= 1 + 2j by induction, so for any M the Archimedean n with |M|^2 < n yields g_n^2 >= 1 + 2n > n > |M|^2 and hence g_k >= g_n > M for all k >= n, i.e. divergence to +infinity; a convergent sequence is bounded, so no contraction constant can exist by thm-contractive-implies-cauchy. The remark's ratio computation also checks: d_{j+1}/d_j = g_j/g_{j+1} = g_j^2/(g_j^2 + 1) < 1 and tends to 1. Blast radius nil: zero deps consumers corpus-wide. Recorded for Alpha as a borderline - ai-altered is defensible if Alpha judges the recurrence itself to carry the claim.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-05"}
