research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:20:{"id":"ex-derivatives-of-polynomials-computed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/der_chapter.html"],"rationale":"The source supplies the power and algebra rules underlying polynomial differentiation. The particular displayed polynomial computations and their stepwise derivation are worked specializations.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:21:{"id":"cex-absolute-value-is-not-differentiable-at-zero","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.mcgill.ca/gantumur/math248f19/differentiation.pdf"],"rationale":"The source gives the absolute-value function as the standard continuous function not differentiable at zero, with conflicting one-sided difference quotients. The proof expands that computation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:22:{"id":"ex-x-cubed-is-strictly-increasing-with-a-vanishing-derivative","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.mcgill.ca/gantumur/math248f19/differentiation.pdf","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter gives x cubed as strictly increasing while its derivative vanishes at zero and records the inverse consequence. The McGill notes support the derivative framework and cubic derivative only, not the strict-increase attribution. The item verifies the properties using the library's power, monotonicity, and inverse results.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:23:{"id":"ex-chain-rule-computed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/der_chapter.html"],"rationale":"The source gives the chain rule and power-rule examples. The item’s chosen composite-polynomial calculation and fully cited factorization are a local worked specialization.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
