research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:25:{"id":"cex-mean-value-theorem-fails-without-continuity-at-the-endpoints","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_mvt.html"],"rationale":"The source identifies endpoint continuity as part of the mean value theorem. The item supplies a simple endpoint-modified affine witness and computes why no mean-value point exists.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:26:{"id":"cex-fermat-fails-at-an-endpoint","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_mvt.html"],"rationale":"The source restricts Fermat’s theorem to interior extrema. The item gives the canonical identity-function endpoint counterexample and checks the nonzero derivative.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
