research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:28:{"id":"cex-differentiable-with-unbounded-derivative-is-not-lipschitz","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.785/2021fa/LectureNotes19.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter supports the bounded-derivative implication. MIT's notes explicitly give the square-root function on $[0,1]$ as non-Lipschitz via an unbounded difference-quotient sequence. The item punctures the endpoint to $(0,1]$ and proves both the unbounded derivative and the punctured-domain Lipschitz contradiction locally.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:29:{"id":"cex-cauchy-mean-value-quotient-form-needs-a-nonvanishing-derivative","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The source states Cauchy’s theorem safely in cross-multiplied form. The item constructs a polynomial example where the denominator derivative vanishes, so the informal quotient form is undefined.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:44:{"id":"fs-bounded-implies-riemann-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch11.pdf","https://ocw.mit.edu/ans7870/18/18.013a/textbook/HTML/chapter20/section04.html"],"rationale":"The sources use the bounded Dirichlet indicator to show boundedness alone does not imply Riemann integrability. The item formulates and refutes that standard false statement via Darboux sums.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:45:{"id":"fs-integrability-is-equivalent-to-a-nowhere-dense-discontinuity-set","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://web.math.princeton.edu/~js129/PDFs/teaching/MAT425_spring_2025/MAT425_Lecture_Notes.pdf","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch11.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources combine Lebesgue’s criterion with a positive-measure nowhere-dense fat Cantor set. The item uses its indicator to refute the proposed nowhere-dense characterization.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:46:{"id":"fs-nonnegative-integrable-with-zero-integral-vanishes","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~gravner/MAT125B/materials/disc3.pdf"],"rationale":"The source establishes that Thomae’s nonnegative function is Riemann integrable with integral zero although it is not identically zero. The item packages this as a counterexample to the false pointwise conclusion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
