research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:48:{"id":"ex-integral-of-x-squared-from-the-definition","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch11.pdf"],"rationale":"The source computes the lower and upper sums for x squared on uniform partitions and obtains integral one third. The item expands the finite-sum algebra in the library’s notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:49:{"id":"ex-refinement-improves-the-darboux-sums","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_rint.html","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch11.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give refinement monotonicity and standard Darboux-sum computations. The exact x-squared partitions and numerical comparison are a local worked example.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:50:{"id":"ex-integral-of-the-floor-function","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://users.math.msu.edu/users/seal/teaching/sp14/hw1.pdf"],"rationale":"The university exercise treats the floor function’s Riemann integrability and integral by integer subintervals. The item specializes to its chosen interval and spells out the Darboux sums.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:51:{"id":"ex-indicator-of-the-cantor-set-is-integrable-with-integral-zero","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://web.math.princeton.edu/~js129/PDFs/teaching/MAT425_spring_2025/MAT425_Lecture_Notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The lecture notes state that the Cantor-set indicator is Riemann integrable with integral zero. The item verifies its discontinuity set and applies Lebesgue’s criterion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
