research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:53:{"id":"cex-dirichlet-is-not-riemann-integrable","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/ch11.pdf","https://ocw.mit.edu/ans7870/18/18.013a/textbook/HTML/chapter20/section04.html"],"rationale":"The sources show that every interval contains rationals and irrationals, forcing lower sums zero and upper sums one for the Dirichlet indicator. The item reproduces that standard proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
